<title>ESTONIA: DANISH-ESTONIAN ENERGY SAVING PROGRAMME SIGNED.</title>
<headline>DANISH-ESTONIAN ENERGY SAVING PROGRAMME SIGNED.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>An Estonian-Danish agreement on energy conservation in the housing and building sector worth six million kroons was signed on Friday in Tallinn, the Danish embassy said.</p>
<p>The agreement for 1997-9 will cover projects such as developing a framework to improve energy efficiency, the embassy said in a statement.</p>
<p>The programme includes public awareness activities and demonstrations of new materials and methods in energy conservation.</p>
<p>In 1996, the Danish government gave nine million kroons in assistance to energy conservation projects in Estonia.</p>
<p>--David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
